+When the title bar is shown by `[appearance.title_bar] mode` or a window rule, dragging empty server-side title bar space moves a window without a modifier. Double-click it to maximize or restore. Floating windows resize by dragging the frame's edges or corners with the left button without a modifier, whether or not the Umbriel title bar is shown. This also works for individually floated windows in tiling layouts. Tiled windows resize by dragging the border between two tiles while Mod is held: a left drag that starts within a few pixels of a tile edge, or in the gap between tiles, resizes the split, and the pointer shows the resize cursor there. A Mod+left drag anywhere else still moves the window, and Mod+right-drag resizes from anywhere in the tile's outer third. Panels and shell chrome still receive clicks while Mod is held, so bar buttons such as the workspace mode switch work with Mod down. The resize cursor follows the same rule: it appears over a tile border or in the gap between tiles, and returns to the normal pointer over the bar, panels, and the empty desktop. Application content and client-side resize controls keep their normal pointer behavior. These compositor-owned interactions work with `client_window_drag = false`.
 
 Title bar presses keep the normal cursor until the pointer crosses a threshold of 10 logical pixels from its position at the original button press. Umbriel then starts dragging and switches to the grabbing cursor. Movement before an application's move request counts toward that threshold. If the pointer has already crossed it, dragging starts immediately without requiring another motion event or another threshold.
 
